Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.3.0-0

%labels
    Maintainer sdweave2@ncsu.edu
    Source https://github.com/ksamuk/pixy
    Version 2.2.4

%help
    pixy — a command-line tool for painlessly computing unbiased estimators
    of population genetic summary statistics that measure genetic variation
    within (pi, Watterson's theta, Tajima's D) and between (dxy, Fst)
    populations from a VCF. pixy is specifically designed to handle VCFs
    containing invariant (monomorphic) sites, which are essential for
    correctly computing pi and dxy in the presence of missing data.

    Usage:
        apptainer run pixy.sif pixy --stats pi fst dxy \
            --vcf <input.vcf.gz> \
            --populations <populations.txt> \
            --window_size 10000 \
            --output_folder <output_dir> \
            --output_prefix <prefix>

    Key options:
        --stats           One or more of: pi, fst, dxy, watterson_theta, tajima_d
        --vcf             bgzip-compressed, tabix/csi-indexed input VCF
        --populations     Tab-separated file mapping sample IDs to population IDs
        --window_size     Size of sliding windows (bp)
        --bed_file        Use BED intervals instead of fixed windows
        --n_cores         Number of parallel cores to use
        --output_folder   Directory for output files
        --output_prefix   Prefix for output file names

    Example:
        apptainer run pixy.sif pixy --help

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e
    set -o pipefail
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # Hazel bind-mount points
    mkdir -p /rs1 /share /home /usr/local/usrapps

    # pixy is distributed via conda-forge (see README badges) — use
    # miniforge3 + mamba, never continuumio/miniconda3 + classic conda
    # (CLAUDE.md lesson 2: classic conda's solver can hang indefinitely on
    # the combined bioconda+conda-forge index).
    mamba create -n pixy -y -c conda-forge -c bioconda pixy=2.2.4
    mamba clean -afy

%environment
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export PATH="/opt/conda/envs/pixy/bin:${PATH}"

%runscript
    exec pixy "$@"

%test
    pixy --help
